WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.208
How well did our theories do?

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.895
Equilibrium theory fits Surtsey in outline, but seabirds moved the equilibrium.

00:00:09.895 --> 00:00:14.939
The General Dynamic Model describes Surtsey's shrinking and the Pitcairn chain,

00:00:14.939 --> 00:00:16.855
but not continental fragments.

00:00:16.855 --> 00:00:21.516
The island rule holds for gecko body size on Socotra, but not head shape.

00:00:21.516 --> 00:00:26.944
And Darwin's subsidence explains Funafuti, while Henderson shows the reverse: uplift.

00:00:28.044 --> 00:00:30.766
And the ethical question applies everywhere.

00:00:30.766 --> 00:00:35.467
In every case, the most-cited knowledge was produced by visiting scientists.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:39.921
Ask where islanders were: as authors, collaborators, or decision-makers.
